# Pin line endings for this repository.
#
# This matters more than usual here: the whole project exists because a line
# ending mismatch broke things. sqlx computes migration checksums from the raw
# bytes of the .sql files, and the patch in patches/ must apply cleanly.
#
# Note the important asymmetry, documented in docs/incident-org-settings.md:
#   * THIS repository is stored with LF.
#   * The OpenAI *source tree* being patched needs its
#     codex-rs/state/*_migrations/*.sql files as CRLF, because that is how
#     OpenAI publishes them and how their checksums were computed.
#     scripts/fix-migrations-crlf.py enforces that at build time.
#     Do NOT "fix" that by adding a .gitattributes rule to the codex checkout.

# Default: normalize to LF in the repository, LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The patch must stay LF or `git apply` fails on some setups.
*.patch text eol=lf

# Windows launchers: CRLF in the working tree so cmd.exe is happy.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# PowerShell prefers CRLF on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary-ish artifacts that must never be normalized.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.gz  binary
*.lib binary
*.pdb binary
